<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry the Lion</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry the Lion was a Welf prince, Duke of Saxony from 1142 and Duke of Bavaria from 1156, the most powerful German noble of his age.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-proud"><span class="enc-name">Henry the Proud</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry the Proud was a Welf prince who was Duke of Bavaria from 1126 and Duke of Saxony from 1137.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-townsend"><span class="enc-name">Henry Townsend</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Townsend was an English missionary of the Church Missionary Society who worked among the Yoruba from the 1840s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-the-fat"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-v-the-fat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry V the Fat</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry V the Fat was a Silesian Piast duke of Legnica from 1278 and also of Wrocław from 1290.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-count-palatine-of-the-rhine"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-v-count-palatine-of-the-rhine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry V, Count Palatine of the Rhine</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry of Brunswick, the eldest son of Henry the Lion, became count palatine of the Rhine in 1195 through his marriage to Agnes, heiress of Conrad of Hohenstaufen.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-v-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry V, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry V, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg, known as Henry the Younger, ruled the Principality of Wolfenbüttel from 1514.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-v-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry V, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry V was the last Salian King of Germany, from 1106, and Holy Roman Emperor from 1111.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-vi-the-good"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-vi-the-good.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry VI the Good</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry VI the Good was a Piast duke of Wrocław in Silesia from 1311.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-vi-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-vi-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry VI, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry VI was a Hohenstaufen emperor, son of Frederick Barbarossa, crowned emperor in 1191.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-england"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry VII of England</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry VII, born Henry Tudor at Pem